    description: "From the WI-kosup reader census (2026-10-28; /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/kosup_reader_census_10282026/B_meta.md §2.1). linkers/registry.py SYNTHETIC_FRAMEWORK_ROLES (~:1172) is a hand-written subset of the framework_role meta-value vocabulary that drifted: 6 of its 15 values are never written, and the IPC linkers write values it lacks -- linkers/ipc.py ~:541 and linkers/phoenix_ipc.py ~:328 write framework_role f\"ipc_{pattern.type}\", i.e. \"ipc_send\" / \"ipc_receive\" (an f-string, emit shape 4), while the set has ipc_publisher / ipc_subscriber. Verified by the orchestrator in the pinned tree. Consequence (STATIC ONLY, not run on a repo): _is_synthetic_node is False for those Electron/Phoenix IPC stand-ins, so whatever keys on it (enclosing-function attachment) skips them. Fix: derive the set from the producers' declared values (or register the framework_role value vocabulary) and add a partition test; measure on an Electron and a Phoenix repo before/after."  # 4aa9
    fields: {}  # 4aa9
