  message: "Fixed in PR #1926 (dev 48fce4044a). SYNTHETIC_FRAMEWORK_ROLES is now one half of a partition of every framework_role the linkers write (18 call-site roles attached; NOT_ENCLOSED_FRAMEWORK_ROLES names the other 8 with reasons; dispatcher marked not reviewed), and every kind=call_site node is a stand-in. ipc.py / phoenix_ipc.py share an IPC_FRAMEWORK_ROLES table instead of the f-string. test_synthetic_role_partition reads the linker sources. Behavioral evidence, survey before/after: session-desktop enclosure edges 125 -> 381, all 43 ipc_send/ipc_receive and every message_*, crypto_*, http_client stand-in now reached from a real symbol (0 before), all 262 new edges span-contained; livebook 327 -> 477, all 31 ipc_* now reached; 38 source-file edges span-contained, 112 start in tier-filtered static/assets bundles via external_symbol placeholders (dev already had 5,876 there) -- filed as WI-zuzud. Production-path tests: the Electron and Phoenix linkers through _connect_synthetic_to_enclosing attach ipcRenderer.send / broadcast! to their function."  # 8bc9
